; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; bonded_incident_urge (PR-A-7 V1, 2026-05-28).
;
; First organic caller of PR-A-5's (urge ...) effect verb. A legacy-aim
; parent with a substantial value-rift against their adult child
; applies an urge - a non-verbal-or-verbal pressure to atone. The urge
; effect:
;   - builds the inner phrase {victim atone _};
;   - mints {actor urge <inner>} in both actor's and victim's minds
;     (the urge anchor; appraisal categorization runs from this);
;   - rolls success against persuasiveness x deference x
;     value_rift_term; on a hit, additionally mints {victim atone _}
;     directly on victim's mind.
;
; The 4-arg urge form (urge ?mother ?son avoid ?girl) is what the plan's
; canonical class-interloper example uses. Reaching that shape needs a
; third role binding the romantic partner (the avoid-target); this V1
; uses the 3-arg form (urge ?actor ?victim atone) which composes
; cleanly with two roles and exercises the urge-verb / value_rift_term
; substrate. The 4-arg path lands when a follow-up event binds the
; partner as a separate role.
;
; Gating shape:
;   - actor: holds {@self life_aim legacy_aim} - legacy-minded parents
;     are the canonical urge senders; other life_aim mixes urge less.
;   - victim: actor's child AND value_rift >= 0.25. value_rift reads
;     held value beliefs (chastity / piety / sobriety) on both
;     parties; a 0.25 floor means at least one disagreement out of
;     three. (`class` was on the value list but no such kind is
;     declared in the ontology - dropped from value-rift entirely;
;     restore when value-belief content events land.) The cooldown
;     isn't checked here - annual cadence is its own backoff.
;   - chance dilutes the per-actor / per-victim rate.
;
; Schedule: annually september (after the betrothal / wedding season,
; when the year's value-mismatch surface is freshest).
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

(include "../shared/roles.hse")

(hsim-event bonded_incident_urge
  (nl       "?actor urges ?victim to atone")
  (kind     _bonded_incident_urge)
  (schedule (annually september))
  (rng-stream incidents)

  (roles
    (role ?actor  (template any_human)
                  (= (situation ?actor life_aim) legacy_aim)
                  (chance 0.10))
    (role ?victim (template any_human)
                  (not (= ?victim ?actor))
                  (believes ?actor {@self child ?victim})
                  (> (value-rift ?actor ?victim) 0.24)
                  (chance 0.30)))

  (effects
    (urge ?actor ?victim atone)
    (log _bonded_incident_urge ?actor)))
